  "independentFinding": "Retain the affirmative APHIS containment statement. It is stronger than quarantine omission, but its geographic and diagnostic scope cannot become biological absence throughout all Washington counties under the current methods.",
  "limitations": [
    "The warning about nonregulated fields is material.",
    "A single morphologically and DNA-confirmed Globodera pallida cyst may remain regulatory Suspect below the two-cyst infestation threshold. No infested field does not imply no detection.",
    "Morphological suspects and inconclusive findings preserve uncertainty. Eradication is a program objective, not a completed determination.",
    "Potato-producing areas cannot silently expand to every habitat. Dormant cysts can remain viable for 30 years.",
    "Florida photograph credits are not occurrence localities. No specific outside-Idaho detection was identified in this retained HTML, but linked documents were not reviewed."
  ],
